  bootwright / cluster exec
      Run a command over SSH on cluster nodes' Machines. By default, log in with the Machine's
      SSH identity. For a different account, supply --ssh-user <user> and --ssh-id-file
      <private-key>. That account must already accept the corresponding public key. An unproved
      host key requires interactive confirmation before SSH offers a credential. The exit
      status is the client's. Bootwright flags go before the command. Use -- before a
      flag-shaped first payload value to preserve it as data. After the first payload value,
      all remaining tokens belong to the payload. --name takes a comma-separated list, and each
      cluster runs the command on the Machine behind its administrator node. --node takes a
      comma-separated list and selects those nodes, by name then by FQDN, in every listed
      cluster that declares them. The command runs on every resolved Machine concurrently, at
      most eight at a time, each output line is prefixed by its Machine, and the exit status is
      the highest any client returned. For an OpenShiftCluster, the default is its first node
      in name order, and --node also accepts <role>-<ordinal> with a zero-based ordinal in that
      order (for example, controlPlane-0 or worker-0). External CephClusters are inapplicable.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster exec <command>... [flags]

  Command flags
      --name  Select comma-separated cluster names (required)
      --node  Select declared nodes by comma-separated name, then FQDN (default: each cluster's
              administrator node)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright cluster exec --context lab --name storage -- uname -a
